# PriceSaver

Telegram price-tracking bot: `PriceSaver.Server` (ASP.NET Core, .NET 9) + `pricesaver.client` (React/TS). Users subscribe to product URLs; parsers re-check prices; Telegram notifies on change.

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root for layout, stack, and conventions.

## Adding a store

When the task is a new retailer, shop, parser, or scraper, follow `.cursor/skills/add-store/SKILL.md` before editing. Required together: `StoreType` enum, `IPriceParser`, `Program.cs` `AddPriceParserHttpClient<TParser>`, `SubscriptionService.InferStoreType`, Telegram store-list copy, docs, and tests. `parser.StoreType` alone is not persisted. Do not register with `AddHttpClient<IPriceParser, T>`.

## Do

- Match existing parser/DI/test patterns (ATB, Silpo, Maudau, METRO).
- Keep Telegram user-facing strings in Ukrainian.
- Use offline `StubHttpMessageHandler` tests; never hit live shops.

## Don't

- Hardcode Telegram tokens or job API keys.
- Add a parser without the enum + `InferStoreType` case + Telegram instructions update.
- Refactor `InferStoreType` or unrelated files in the same change unless asked.
